Protocol Target Lab IGMP membership holder, query peer and typed kernel-link
helper use autonomous MIT project code and the Python standard library.
The source never sends a raw IGMP Report. Membership reports are generated by
the actual running Linux kernel, which is shared by Docker containers rather
than provided as a new guest kernel or user-space protocol stack in this image.

The pinned Python base retains CPython LICENSE at
/usr/local/lib/python3.12/LICENSE.txt and OS copyright notices under /usr/share/doc.
Wrapper MIT terms do not replace those licenses. Offline wrapper rebuilding
requires the matching prepared fixed base cache; this is not complete OS/kernel
source distribution. iproute2 is a host package dependency for the narrow helper,
not copied from an unknown host binary into this runtime.
